{title: Adonai}
{artist: Amy Denson}
{genre: Modern Worship}
{style: Ballad}
{flow: Meditative, Response}
{key: D}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}
{license: WorshipCommons License 1.0}
{copyright: © 2008 Amy Denson}
{c: © 2008 Amy Denson · WorshipCommons License 1.0 (free for worship) https://worshipcommons.org/license · Source: https://worshipcommons.org/songs/adonai-bQThg8R1Grk/}
{c: Chords: the writer's own chart}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dsus2]Father look down upon Your [Cadd9]servants
[Dsus2]May we find favor in Your [Cadd9]eyes
[Dsus2]Help us to comprehend Your [Cadd9]holiness
And Your [G]nature, Most High [Dsus2]God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dsus2]Take from us all of our [Cadd9]complacency
[Dsus2]Consume us with zeal for Your [Cadd9]house
[Dsus2]Help us to love the things that [Cadd9]You love
And to [G]hate what is against Your [Dsus2]heart [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
May Your [G]holiness [D]consume us
Your [G]righteousness, may it [D]reign in us
[Cadd9]Come and bring Your fire [G]into our very hearts
[Cadd9]Take out every part of us that [G]isn’t just like You [D]are [Cadd9]
Father, just like You [Dsus2]are
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Ado[Cadd9]nai, [G]reign in my [Dsus2]heart
[D]Oh, Ado[Cadd9]nai, my [G]ruler and my [Dsus2]God
[D]Ado[Cadd9]nai, I [G]bow before Your [Dsus2]throne
[D]Oh, Ado[Cadd9]nai, my [G]heart is all Your [Dsus2]own
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dsus2]No one can look upon Your [Cadd9]face and live
So [Dsus2]let us see Your face and [Cadd9]die
Your [Dsus2]lovingkindness will [Cadd9]raise us up
Into [G]everlasting [Dsus2]life [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus 2}
May Your [G]holiness [D]consume us
Your [G]righteousness, may it [D]reign in us
[Cadd9]Come and bring Your fire [G]into our very hearts
[Cadd9]Take out every part of us that [G]isn’t just like You [D]are [Cadd9]
Father, just like You [Dsus2]are
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Ending (a cappella)}
Adonai, reign in my heart
Oh Adonai, my ruler and my God
Adonai, I bow before Your throne
Oh Adonai, my heart is all Your own
{end_of_verse}
